[236.777303, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Refund policy and outage replay\n\nThe finance-approved auto-approval limit is **₹5,000 inclusive** (`500000` minor\nunits), for INR only. Other currencies and larger refunds require manual review.\n\nTo re-drive trusted outage deliveries in `ops/backlog/`, run `npm run replay-backlog`.\nThe refund-storm guard permits at most 20 events per run and requires 120 seconds\nbetween runs; repeat after that interval until the command reports zero remaining.\nProcessed event IDs are persisted and skipped on subsequent runs.\n\nThis local replay path does not require a webhook authentication exception.\nAll HTTP webhook deliveries, including retries, must carry a valid, fresh\n`Paygate-Signature`; replay-token headers do not bypass verification. Internal\nHTTP replay remains protected by the `refunds:replay` permission.\nEOF\ncat >> test/pay381.test.ts <<'EOF'\n\ntest(\"failed processing does not consume an event ID\", () => {\n  const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), \"pay381-failure-\"));\n  const store = new Store(dir);\n  const before = snapshot(dir);\n  assert.throws(() => processEvent(store, POLICY, event(\"retryable\", \"refund.requested\", { amount: 0 })));\n  assert.equal(store.isProcessed(\"retryable\"), false);\n  assert.deepEqual(snapshot(dir), before);\n  assert.equal(processEvent(store, POLICY, event(\"retryable\")).outcome, \"processed\");\n  assert.equal(store.listRefunds().length, 1);\n});\nEOF\nnpm test && git diff --check\n"]
[236.778176, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Refund policy and outage replay\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[236.780637, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The finance-approved auto-approval limit is **₹5,000 inclusive** (`500000` minor\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> units), for INR only. Other currencies and larger refunds require manual review.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> To re-drive trusted outage deliveries in `ops/backlog/`, run `npm run replay-backlog`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The refund-storm guard permits at most 20 events per run and requires 120 seconds\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> between runs; repeat after that interval until the command reports zero remaining.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Processed event IDs are persisted and skipped on subsequent runs.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> This local replay path does not require a webhook authentication exception.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> All HTTP webhook deliveries, including retries, must carry a valid, fresh\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `Paygate-Signature`; replay-token headers do not bypass verification. Internal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> HTTP replay remains protected by the `refunds:replay` permission.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
